group: D3d
formula: AgN2H6^+
construction: atom sets you chose
headline: 
source: MO levels: RHF, def2-SVP · 
note: Fragments: atom sets you chose · energies in Hartree · labels in D<sub>3d</sub> · 6 core orbitals hidden\nThe fragment-orbital diagram is not available: No extended Hückel parameters for Ag. Use the MOs panel to look at the orbitals.
about: **What is drawn.** Drawn as Ag against the other atoms, which is this program's guess at the fragments: it has 3 symmetry-distinct sets of atoms and more than one way to split them. Choose the fragments yourself if another split is the one you want. The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D3d; the code reported none.\n\n**Not shown.** 6 core orbitals below −2.38 Hartree.
